<title>SPAIN: Spain still has room to cut rates - minister.</title>
<headline>Spain still has room to cut rates - minister.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Industry Minister Josep Pique said on Thursday a fall in interest rates is possible after the dramatic fall seen in the past year in the long term cash yield spread between Spanish and German bonds.</p>
<p>&quot;This (fall in the spread) suggests that our country still has room to cut interest rates,&quot; Pique told reporters at a conference.</p>
<p>The Bank of Spain's key money rate is currently at 6.00 percent. -- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
